1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,569
Welcome to 3D Viewer.

2
00:00:01,629 --> 00:00:06,953
This app puts real, interactive 3D models
on your Shopify storefront — no code, no

3
00:00:07,013 --> 00:00:10,629
separate hosting, and no theme editing
beyond one block.

4
00:00:11,839 --> 00:00:13,037
This is the end result.

5
00:00:13,097 --> 00:00:17,465
A shopper lands on the product page and
can drag the model to spin it, zoom in on

6
00:00:17,525 --> 00:00:19,543
the stitching, and open it fullscreen.

7
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:23,643
On a phone they can even place it in their
own room with augmented reality.

8
00:00:24,503 --> 00:00:27,175
Let's start where the app opens: the
dashboard.

9
00:00:27,985 --> 00:00:32,009
When you open 3D Viewer from your Shopify
admin, this is the home screen.

10
00:00:32,069 --> 00:00:36,484
Your store name sits under the title, and
your current plan is in the top right.

11
00:00:37,344 --> 00:00:41,970
This row is the whole app. Product 3D
Models attaches a model to a product.

12
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:46,093
3D Model Library holds standalone models
you can drop on any page.

13
00:00:46,153 --> 00:00:49,217
Documentation, Pricing and Setup do what
they say.

14
00:00:50,077 --> 00:00:52,938
If you're new, the Getting started card is
your route.

15
00:00:52,998 --> 00:00:57,049
Three steps: create the metafield
definitions, upload your first model, then

16
00:00:57,109 --> 00:00:58,130
add the theme block.

17
00:00:58,190 --> 00:01:02,674
Each one ticks green on its own once it's
genuinely done — the app checks your store

18
00:01:02,734 --> 00:01:05,432
rather than remembering that you clicked
something.

19
00:01:06,292 --> 00:01:08,265
Four tiles summarise where you stand.

20
00:01:08,325 --> 00:01:11,726
Products with a model shows your coverage
across the catalogue.

21
00:01:11,786 --> 00:01:14,199
Models in use counts against your plan
limit.

22
00:01:14,259 --> 00:01:18,264
Uploads this month is your recent
activity, and the last tile is your plan

23
00:01:18,324 --> 00:01:19,748
with a shortcut to billing.

24
00:01:20,608 --> 00:01:23,221
That second tile is worth a closer look.

25
00:01:23,281 --> 00:01:27,566
It counts distinct model files, not
assignments. So if the same .

26
00:01:27,626 --> 00:01:32,980
glb is attached to a product and also sits
in your library, it uses one slot, not

27
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:33,640
two.

28
00:01:34,107 --> 00:01:38,399
Scrolling down, Recently added models
lists your latest uploads with size and

29
00:01:38,459 --> 00:01:41,452
date — click any row to jump straight into
that model.

30
00:01:41,512 --> 00:01:45,691
Underneath, Upload activity charts what
you've added, and you can switch it

31
00:01:45,751 --> 00:01:47,273
between day, week and month.

32
00:01:48,133 --> 00:01:52,939
On the right, Quick links jump to the
other sections, and File types breaks down

33
00:01:52,999 --> 00:01:56,467
the formats in your library — handy for
spotting a stray .

34
00:01:56,527 --> 00:01:58,656
gltf when you meant to upload . glb.

35
00:01:59,516 --> 00:02:04,268
At the very bottom, Help and resources
gives you the video tutorial, the built-in

36
00:02:04,328 --> 00:02:06,882
documentation, and a direct line to
support.

37
00:02:07,742 --> 00:02:09,743
Here's the whole app in four steps.

38
00:02:09,803 --> 00:02:14,633
Setup once, upload a model, add the block
once, then tune the viewer as much as you

39
00:02:14,693 --> 00:02:15,293
like.

40
00:02:14,987 --> 00:02:18,579
Everything else in this series is detail
on one of those four.

41
00:02:19,439 --> 00:02:20,586
That's the dashboard.

42
00:02:20,646 --> 00:02:25,297
Next up, the Setup page — the one screen
you have to visit before anything reaches

43
00:02:25,357 --> 00:02:26,216
your storefront.
